From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:22:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: identify block undo reader failures with typed
 positions

Retain non-dropping Error, complete static/function messages and the old
cold-path FlatFilePos text. Open failures additionally expose signed file
number and unsigned offset. Exception details use the existing bounded
copied Error field/truncation contract. No new formatter or adapter API.

Add a focused public ReadBlockUndo case using an independent manager and
owned temporary records. Exercise unavailable undo, missing file, empty
record deserialization and deliberately mismatched checksum, then correct
only the checksum and require a successful read. Check actual event names,
messages, numeric position fields and unchanged reader return values.
No private hook, chain state mutation, production data or UTXO rule changes.

Shared eCash block-storage owner. Source-only event lint/diff checks pass;
new native case NOT_COMPILED/NOT_RUN. Synthetic empty records test reader
integrity only, not block connection. Sealed381/current intake unchanged.

